    "html": "Not the entire list of changes.<br><br>AI RELATED :<br>- Changes to the AI budgeting to prevent them running out of cash and steam if they suffer a little setback<br>- Changes to try to make the AI expand more \"coherently\"<br><br>BALANCE RELATED :<br>- Emperors can now recruit Militia lines \"upgrades\" (ex : Ji Infantry/Heavy Ji Infantry) at level 1 on their characters. Dragon units moved to rank 6 when Emperor as well.<br>- Removed tradeoffs on prestige points.<br>- Added a small tradeoff on the first prestige rank that reduces construction cost but also reduce income you get from buildings to help player get going in the early game.<br>- You now get 2 assignements instead of 1 for most effects (techs/prestige/faction rank)<br>- Some of the existing foreign assignments were buffed.<br>- When Emperor, you only get 1 extra factionwide effect position instead of extra 4. (so you get 4 in total instead of 7)<br>- Reach movement range removed completely. Instead now provides reinforcement range.<br>- Consideration (Champion skill that provided reinforcement range) now provides a bit of supplies.<br>- Supply penalty on foreign soil \"flattened\" to be the \"Normal\" difficulty value of -20 (instead of -40 in Legendary)<br>- No more movement range penalty when in foreign territory. (this is also to help the AI)<br><br>- Governors shouldn't reduce corruption anymore. (Work in progress as I've unfortunately forgotten about the special governor positions)<br><br>NEW STUFF :<br>- There are now new \"foreign\" assignments. For you to gain advantages over the enemy (because I don't think the AI is smart enough to use them lmao)<br><br>TWEAKS :<br>- Tweaked some of the texts on some of the court positions. (Some parts of this are still WIP as they require tweaks in the main mod)<br>- Nerfs to the Han economy buildings to try and clean up superfluous effects. This will mean tighter food and public order.",
